<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<action_sets>
	<!-- Dwarf creature-mount riders: the warg, spider, elephant and chariot rider rows of as_human_warrior, merged into
	     the dwarf sets. When an agent rides, the engine looks the mount's usage actions up in the rider's set for the
	     rider's pose. LOTRLOME_Armory adds them to as_human_warrior only (the warg and spider rows in a partial at the
	     top of its action_sets.xml, the elephant and chariot rows through action_sets.xslt), and as_dwarf_warrior has
	     no base_set, so a dwarf on a free warg had none (the game crashed when one mounted, owner report 2026-11-14;
	     the crash point itself is not logged). The dwarf set already plays the human horse-rider clips (rider_horse_*),
	     so the human rider clips are used as they are. The female set took its base_set copy before this merge and
	     gets the same block. The xslt's act_horse_jump_* and act_howdah_* rows are left out: they would replace the
	     dwarf's horse jumps. DwarfMountRiderRowsTests pins these rows to the Armory's. -->
	<action_set id="as_dwarf_warrior">
